.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt AUDIO-OUTPUT-DEVICES 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm audio-output-devices
.Nd list playable audio outputs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints one line per playable output, ordered by pcm unit:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pcm kind sink description
.Ed
.Pp
.Ar pcm
is the unit number.
.Ar kind
is
.Cm speakers
or
.Cm headphones .
A description that names the internal analog output or the
built-in speakers is
.Cm speakers .
Every other playback device is
.Cm headphones ,
including a headphone jack, a USB adapter, and dock audio.
.Ar sink
is the Pulse sink name,
.Cm oss_output.dsp Ns Ar pcm .
.Ar description
is the rest of the line.
.Pp
When
.Xr pactl 1
can reach a daemon,
.Nm
loads
.Cm module-oss
for each playable
.Pa /dev/dsp Ns Ar N
that does not already have that sink.
When Pulse has no such sinks, the list is taken from
.Pa /dev/sndstat .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/sndstat"
.It Pa /dev/sndstat
Playback devices used when Pulse has no
.Cm oss_output.dsp Ns Ar N
sink.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr audio-output-toggle 1 ,
.Xr pactl 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
